      "slug": "cereal-production-is-1-5x-higher-than-in-1972",
      "title": "The Food Shortage Forecast Missed The Harvest",
      "hook": "The world was told food would run out. The numbers disagree.",
      "says": [
        "In 1985, secondary-school progression was 77.8 percent; by 2017, 91.3—1.2 times higher.",
        "In 1972, cereal production was 1083.7 million metric tons; by 2024, 1644.1 million—1.5 times higher.",
        "China leads: 5.2 million square kilometers; United States 4.2, Australia 3.6, Brazil 2.4, Russia 2.2."
      ],
      "closing": "The feared famine never arrived as predicted.",
      "question": "Which changed more: school, grain, or land?"
    },
    {
      "slug": "combustible-renewables-and-waste-is-3-0x-higher-than-in-1990",
      "title": "Waste Energy Tripled—And It Isn’t Solar",
      "hook": "One energy source tripled, and it was mostly waste.",
      "says": [
        "In 1990, combustible renewables and waste was 10.2%; by 2024, 30.1%—3.0 times higher.",
        "In 1998, electricity access was 73.2%; by 2024, 91.9%—1.3 times higher.",
        "In 1972, waste methane (ch4) was 903.8 Mt CO2e; by 2024, 1,652 Mt CO2e—1.8 times higher."
      ],
      "closing": "Waste became a serious part of the energy mix.",
      "question": "Which changed most: fuel, power, or waste?"
    },
    {
      "slug": "population-growth-fell-54-since-1972",
      "title": "Population Growth Didn’t Keep Accelerating",
      "hook": "The population curve changed direction more sharply than expected.",
      "says": [
